new-page: true

= The <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> merges with the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed:<span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?]

Vellt has long been a strong advocate for deepening ties between the two right-wing parties, ultimately aiming for a merger. Even before ascending to the leadership of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, he had been cultivating relations with Trevannon’s Young Conservatives[? if traditionalist_leader == "Lambach":&nbsp;and Lambach's <span style="color: #6D5298;">Faithful Socials</span>?]. With a friendly leadership now in control of the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed:<span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?], the path to unification appears clear.

Most of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> backs Vellt’s merger ambitions, opposed only by a small but vocal left wing around Curtius and Lytton, who insist on preserving the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> as a liberal force. Within the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed:<span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?], resistance stems primarily from its <span style="color: #385A38;">agrarian</span> wing, reluctant to unite with the capitalist, and middle-class oriented <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>. The party’s old guard, led by Westmore, also remains skeptical—citing differences over the national questions.

- @dnvp_dvp: Regardless, an agreement has been reached.

@dnvp_dvp
face-image: img/dvpposter.jpg

With the merger all but finalized, the new party has agreed to call itself the <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span>, or the <span style="color: #00C0FF;">Free Conservative Party</span>, styling itself as the spirital successor to the Empire-era party of the same name.

Many on the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>'s left have defected to the flourishing <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>, seeing it as the last bastion of liberalism. 

If Stratton were alive, he would be quite disappointed in what has become of his liberal party.

- @leadership: The party now needs to elect a leader.

@leadership
