on-arrival: {!
    Q.dhv_fkp = 0;
    Q.fkp_leader = 0;
    Q.fkp_ideology = 0;
    Q.natcons_fkp = 0;
    Q.stressmanites_fkp = 0;
    Q.agrarians_fkp = 0;
    Q.industrialists_fkp = 0;
    Q.pp_conservatives_fkp = 0;
    if (Q.kvp_formed == 0) {
        Q.dhv_fkp = (Q.commons_gold_normalized + Q.commons_traditionalist_normalized + (Q.burgher_traditionalist_normalized*0.5) + (Q.burgher_gold_normalized*0.5)*0.6);
        Q.natcons_fkp = Q.guild_traditionalist_normalized*1.5;
        Q.pp_conservatives_fkp = (Q.burgher_traditionalist_normalized*1.5) + (Q.guild_traditionalist_normalized*1.5);
        Q.stressmanites_fkp = Q.burgher_gold_normalized*0.5;
        Q.industrialists_fkp = Q.guild_gold_normalized;
        Q.agrarians_fkp = Q.landed_traditionalist_normalized*0.7;
    }
    if (Q.kvp_formed == 1) {
        Q.dhv_fkp = (Q.commons_gold_normalized + Q.commons_kvp_normalized + (Q.burgher_kvp_normalized*0.5) + (Q.burgher_gold_normalized*0.5)*0.6);
        Q.natcons_fkp = Q.guild_kvp_normalized*1.5;
        Q.pp_conservatives_fkp = (Q.burgher_kvp_normalized*1.5) + (Q.guild_kvp_normalized*0.5);
        Q.stressmanites_fkp = Q.burgher_gold_normalized*0.5;
        Q.industrialists_fkp = Q.guild_gold_normalized;
        Q.agrarians_fkp = Q.landed_kvp_normalized*0.7;
    }
    if (Q.traditionalist_leader == "Tilford") {
        Q.agrarians_fkp = Q.agrarians_fkp*2;
    }
    if (Q.traditionalist_leader == "Westmore") {
        Q.natcons_fkp = Q.natcons_fkp*2;
    }
    if (Q.traditionalist_leader == "Hargen") {
        Q.natcons_fkp = Q.natcons_fkp*1.5;
        Q.pp_conservatives_fkp = Q.natcons_fkp*1.5;
    }
    if (Q.traditionalist_leader == "Trevannon") {
        Q.natcons_fkp = Q.natcons_fkp*0.7;
        Q.pp_conservatives_fkp = Q.natcons_fkp*2;
    }
    if (Q.traditionalist_leader == "Trevannon") {
        Q.natcons_fkp = Q.natcons_fkp*0.7;
        Q.pp_conservatives_fkp = Q.pp_conservatives_fkp*2;
    }
    if (Q.kvp_formed == 1) {
        Q.pp_conservatives_fkp = Q.pp_conservatives_fkp*2;
        Q.agrarians_fkp = Q.agrarians_fkp*0.8;
        Q.natcons_fkp = Q.natcons_fkp*0.8;
    }
    if (Q.gold_reform == 1) {
        Q.dhv_fkp = Q.dhv_fkp*1.4;
    }
    if (Q.gold_reform == 2) {
        Q.dhv_fkp = Q.dhv_fkp*1.5;
    }
    if (Q.gold_leader == "Mardle" || Q.gold_leader == "Coalfax") {
        Q.industrialists_fkp = Q.industrialists_fkp*1.5;
    }
    if (Q.pro_republic >= 60) {
        Q.pp_conservatives_fkp = Q.pp_conservatives_fkp*1.5;
        Q.stressmanites_fkp = Q.stressmanites_fkp*1.5;
    } else {
        Q.natcons_fkp = Q.natcons_fkp*1.5;
        Q.agrarians_fkp = Q.agrarians_fkp*1.5;
    }
    Q.raumer_points_fkp = Q.industrialists_fkp + Q.stressmanites_fkp*0.5;
    Q.glatzel_points_fkp = Q.dhv_fkp + Q.stressmanites_fkp*0.5;
    Q.westarp_points_fkp = Q.agrarians_fkp*0.6 + Q.natcons_fkp*0.4;
    Q.hergt_points_fkp = Q.agrarians_fkp*0.4 + Q.natcons_fkp*0.6;
    Q.treviranus_points_fkp = Q.pp_conservatives_fkp;
    Q.winner_fkp = "Hargen";
    if (Q.glatzel_points_fkp > Q.raumer_points_fkp && Q.pro_republic > 65) {
        Q.glatzel_points_fkp += Q.raumer_points_fkp;
        Q.raumer_points_fkp = 0;
    } else {
         Q.treviranus_points_fkp += Q.glatzel_points_fkp;
         Q.glatzel_points_fkp == 0;
    }
    if (Q.glatzel_points_fkp + Q.treviranus_points_fkp + Q.raumer_points_fkp > (Q.hergt_points_fkp + Q.westarp_points_fkp)/2) {
        if (Q.pro_republic > 55) {
            Q.hergt_points_fkp += Q.westarp_points_fkp;
            Q.westarp_points_fkp == 0;
        } else {
            Q.westarp_points_fkp += Q.hergt_points_fkp;
            Q.hergt_points_fkp == 0;
        }
    }
    if (Q.raumer_points + Q.treviranus_points_fkp + Q.glatzel_points_fkp > Q.hergt_points_fkp + Q.westarp_points_fkp) {
        if (Q.gold_leader == "Vellt" && Q.raumer_points + Q.glatzel_points_fkp + (Q.treviranus_points_fkp*0.4) > Q.hergt_points_fkp + Q.westarp_points_fkp) {
            Q.winner_fkp = "Vellt";
        } else {
            if (Q.raumer_points_fkp + Q.glatzel_points_fkp > Q.treviranus_points_fkp) {
                Q.winner_fkp = "Raumer";
            } else {
                Q.winner_fkp = "Trevannon";
            }
        }
    } else {
        if ((Q.raumer_points + Q.treviranus_points_fkp + Q.glatzel_points_fkp)*1.1 >= Q.hergt_points_fkp + Q.westarp_points_fkp || Q.hergt_points_fkp > Q.westarp_points_fkp) {
            Q.winner_fkp = "Hargen";
        } else {
            Q.winner_fkp = "Westmore";
        }
    }
!}
go-to: calculations

@calculations
new-page: true

= <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span> Leadership Election

Now that the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> and [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed:<span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?] have merged, the newly formed <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span> must decide who will lead it into this next chapter. Several distinct factions, ranging from industrialists to nationalists to Free Guild members, are already vying for influence within the fledgling party. The election of a chairman at the <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span>’s inaugural congress will determine the internal balance of power and shape their future direction. With its future orientation still fluid, the outcome of the leadership vote may define whether the <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span> leans toward tolerance of the republic or if it embraces a more nationalist course.

Major Factions:

<span style="color: #3E88B3;">National Conservatives</span> ([? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed:<span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?]) [+ natcons_fkp +]

<span style="color: #385A38;">Agrarians</span> ([? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed:<span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?]) [+ agrarians_fkp +]

<span style="color: #8C7A3C;">Industrialists</span> (<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>) [+ industrialists_fkp +]

<hr id="read-marker">

<span style="color: #D8B868;">Right-wing Unions</span> (<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> and [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed:<span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?]) [+ dhv_fkp +]

<span style="color: #D8B868;">Strattonites</span> (<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>) [+ stressmanites_fkp +]

<span style="color: #0087DC;">People's Conservatives</span> ([? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed:<span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?]) [+ ppconservatives_fkp +]

- @glatzel: Florian Vellt.
- @treviranus: Gottfried Trevannon.
- @raumer: Hans von Raumer.
- @hergt: Cuthbert Hargen.
- @westarp: Kuno von Westmore.

@glatzel
subtitle: Hailing from the reformist elements of the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, he seeks to create a unitary force on the right.
choose-if: winner_fkp = "Vellt"
on-arrival: fkp_leader = "Vellt"; fkp_ideology = "Paternalistic Conservatism";
call: dnvp_dvp_formed
face-image: img/portraits/glatzel.jpg

Against expectations, Frank Vellt prevailed in a drawn‑out, multi‑round ballot at the <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span>’s inaugural congress. Centrists like Trevannon and von Raumer were the first to fall in the election, ultimately endorsing Vellt over hard‑line monarchists such as Hargen and Westmore. By the final ballot, Vellt had assembled a coalition of moderate [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed:<span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?] holdouts, white-collar union delegates, and the remaining <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> moderates, clinching the chairmanship despite standing on the party’s left.

This outcome represents the best potential scenario for us, as Vellt remains open to some negotiation with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>. However, the new <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span> will still be a far more obstinate partner than Stratton’s <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, given the enduring influence of agrarian and industrialist factions. Any cooperation will likely be more constrained than in the past. Still, compared to the uncompromising hardliners who nearly won the contest, Vellt’s victory is a relief. 

@raumer
subtitle: Backed by manu prominent industrialists from the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>, von Raumer aims to strengthen the bourgiois.
choose-if: winner_fkp = "Raumer"
on-arrival: fkp_leader = "von-Raumer"; fkp_ideology = "Liberal Conservatism";
call: dnvp_dvp_formed
face-image: img/portraits/von_raumer.jpg

After several rounds of elimination voting at the <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span>’s inaugural congress, Hans von Raumer secured the chairmanship by consolidating the party’s pro‑business wing. The moderate Frank Vellt was the first to fall in the competition. In the penultimate round, Gottfried Trevannon withdrew and threw his support behind von Raumer, rather than the hard‑line monarchists. Industrialists and big‑business delegates, long allied with von Raumer, rallied en masse, joined by former <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> deputies and even some Free Guild members, giving him a decisive edge over Kuno von Westmore in the final ballot.

This represents an interesting development for us. While von Raumer is firmly linked to the industrialist wing of <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span>, he has demonstrated firm support for Unity Coalitions in previous governments. He even has a good working relationship with Vendrin Bell. However, he would still be active in trying to limit our policies in any future government. Additionally, many of his own supporters in the industrialist wing would seek to prevent any coalition with us, so cooperation will still be more difficult than it was with Stratton's <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>. 

@treviranus
subtitle: Trevannon, ardent reformer, and member of the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate":<span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if kvp_formed:<span style="color: #0087DC;">**KVP**</span>?], has put himself forwards.
choose-if: winner_fkp = "Trevannon"
on-arrival: fkp_leader = "Trevannon"; fkp_ideology = "Liberal Conservatism";
call: dnvp_dvp_formed
face-image: img/portraits/Trevannon.jpg

After a protracted, multi‑round ballot at the <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span>’s inaugural congress, Gottfried Trevannon secured the party chairmanship. Building a coalition of moderate <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> dissidents, rural‑Chamber delegates, and a sprinkling of pragmatic ex‑<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> members allowed him to do well in the first round. Frank Vellt, representing the party’s moderates, was the first to be eliminated. Then industrial conservatives around Hans von Raumer, unwilling to back the hard‑line monarchists, shifted en masse to Trevannon by the penultimate ballot, giving him a clear path to the chairmanship against Kuno von Westmore.

Many in our party have signaled their resigned acceptance of Trevannon. While they remain deeply suspicious of his nationalist rhetoric and austere economic agenda, they acknowledge he is less hostile to the Unity order than the outright monarchists within his party. Hopefully, he will act as a bulwark against the rising [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">far</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">far</span>?]-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> in the country.

@hergt
subtitle: A member of the Old Guard of the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span>?], backed by rural and conservative elements.
choose-if: winner_fkp = "Hargen"
on-arrival: fkp_leader = "Hargen"; fkp_ideology = "Liberal Conservatism"; 
call: dnvp_dvp_formed
face-image: img/portraits/OskarHergt.jpg

After several rounds of elimination voting at the <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span>’s inaugural congress, Cuthbert Hargen secured the chairmanship by uniting the party’s monarchist‑conservative wing. The moderate Frank Vellt was the first to go, followed by Hans von Raumer, whose industrialist backers then fragmented between Trevannon and Hargen. In the penultimate round, Kuno von Westmore withdrew and threw his delegates behind Hargen rather than the centrist faction led by Gottfried Trevannon. Agrarian conservatives, church‑aligned delegates, and a sizable bloc of <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> conservatives gave him the edge over Trevannon in the final ballot.

Hargen’s victory has seen our relations with the <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span> sour. His entrenched monarchism and hostility toward democratic processes have already led him to explore increased cooperation with the far right, including informal contacts with the Wardens. Genuine legislative collaboration now seems all but impossible, making building coalitions in the future increasingly difficult.

@westarp
subtitle: A radical right-wing member of the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span>?], seeking to transform the party in a hardline direction.
choose-if: winner_fkp = "Westmore"
on-arrival: fkp_leader = "Westmore"; fkp_ideology = "National Conservatism";
call: dnvp_dvp_formed
face-image: img/portraits/Kuno_von_Westarp.jpg

After several rounds of elimination voting at the <span style="color: #00C0FF;">**FKP**</span>’s inaugural congress, Kuno von Westmore prevailed to win the chairmanship by rallying the party’s rural and ethno‑nationalist wings. The moderate Frank Vellt was the first to be eliminated. In subsequent ballots, moderate conservatives around Hans von Raumer and ex‑<span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span> figures split their votes between Trevannon and Hargen, while Westmore consolidated support from his agrarian‐traditionalist bloc. In the penultimate round, Cuthbert Hargen withdrew and threw his delegates behind Westmore rather than the centerists led by Gottfried Trevannon.

Westmore’s ascension means that the right is now effectively devoid of democratic parties. His explicit blood-purism and paramilitary sympathies signal a dangerous shift toward radical exclusion and street‑tier violence. This will make stabilizing the republic increasingly difficult, as the right increasingly rejects the republic.
